  "description": "This dataset comprises electroencephalography (EEG) recordings from older adults during resting state and auditory oddball task conditions. Participants completed both passive and active oddball tasks under two conditions: a control condition and an arousal condition (threat of unpredictable shock). The dataset includes resting state recordings with eyes open and closed, providing a comprehensive resource for investigating age-related changes in neural responses to auditory stimuli and locus coeruleus-noradrenaline system function under stress.",
